(453832, 42044, 12448, '<td valign="top">Yum!  I would be afraid to pick mushrooms though, my luck I would get the poisonous ones, LOL!  This is a great shot, the light, the DOF is wonderful but the balance seems off to me, the big space in the middle is a bit of a distraction to me, maybe a little different cropping or angle of the shot would have fixe this for me.  I started this at a 6 but am going up to an 8 because the overall shot is very good.</td>', 'Yum!  I would be afraid to pick mushrooms though, my luck I would get the poisonous ones, LOL!  This is a great shot, the light, the DOF is wonderful but the balance seems off to me, the big space in the middle is a bit of a distraction to me, maybe a little different cropping or angle of the shot would have fixe this for me.  I started this at a 6 but am going up to an 8 because the overall shot is very good.', '2003-10-17 12:50:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(453833, 41771, 12448, '<td valign="top">My dog is drooling on my keyboard! :)<br/> <br/>This is an excellent take on the challenge, very unique and managed to get the animal aspect in there, WTG!  The shot is a bit busy, lines here and there and everywhere that the bones are going but the different tones of the bones are very nice and offer wonderful contrast.  I think I would have liked to seen at least one full treat in the shot with the others all over.  I started this one at a 6 but I''m going to an 8, different cropping or angle would have gotten you a 9 or 10</td>', 'My dog is drooling on my keyboard! :) This is an excellent take on the challenge, very unique and managed to get the animal aspect in there, WTG!  The shot is a bit busy, lines here and there and everywhere that the bones are going but the different tones of the bones are very nice and offer wonderful contrast.  I think I would have liked to seen at least one full treat in the shot with the others all over.  I started this one at a 6 but I''m going to an 8, different cropping or angle would have gotten you a 9 or 10', '2003-10-17 12:52:47.000000', NULL, 1),
