(460128, 42074, 9550, '<td valign="top">Thanks to everyone who voted, And to all who left comments. I just didnt have the right lighting to stop the reflection on the Fork and Spoon. Thanks again, and i hope you enjoy the dish. Aubrey<br/> <br/>P.S. I forgot to add the salt and pepper <br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2003-10-23 13:25:36.</i></td>', 'Thanks to everyone who voted, And to all who left comments. I just didnt have the right lighting to stop the reflection on the Fork and Spoon. Thanks again, and i hope you enjoy the dish. Aubrey P.S. I forgot to add the salt and pepper ', '2003-10-23 14:24:32.000000', '2003-10-23 14:25:36.000000', 0),
(460145, 42447, 9550, '<td valign="top">Congrats Mom!!! As JD was saying about the straight on shot, Remember your first photo you sent me (The straight on shot) But you still did really good on this one. Love ya, Aubrey</td>', 'Congrats Mom!!! As JD was saying about the straight on shot, Remember your first photo you sent me (The straight on shot) But you still did really good on this one. Love ya, Aubrey', '2003-10-23 14:33:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(460365, 42469, 12617, '<td valign="top">it was sour cream in the center, unfortunatly a bit runny, but couldn;t be helped.<br/>This was a rushed excersize before work the day it had to be in, and didn;t realise the cream was overexposed till I put it on the computer :( <br/> <br/>There was a knife and fork in the photo, but I had to do some harsh cropping because I did this on a bedside dresser, it was a really dark red wood, and nice reflective.  I wish I had taken some without the fork, I have a ps''d version without the fork and it looks much better and balanced!<br/> <br/>The cashews in the back, they were in a pot I was eating, and the photo was too plain, to I put the pepper in and tipped some of my cashews on the table, I felt it really helped the photo....  but didn''t even think of the ''must be in the dish''.. thanks for pointing that out.</td>', 'it was sour cream in the center, unfortunatly a bit runny, but couldn;t be helped.This was a rushed excersize before work the day it had to be in, and didn;t realise the cream was overexposed till I put it on the computer :(  There was a knife and fork in the photo, but I had to do some harsh cropping because I did this on a bedside dresser, it was a really dark red wood, and nice reflective.  I wish I had taken some without the fork, I have a ps''d version without the fork and it looks much better and balanced! The cashews in the back, they were in a pot I was eating, and the photo was too plain, to I put the pepper in and tipped some of my cashews on the table, I felt it really helped the photo....  but didn''t even think of the ''must be in the dish''.. thanks for pointing that out.', '2003-10-23 18:51:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(460435, 42381, 6458, '<td valign="top">Good show Jason!<br/> <br/>I use the showman''s way of starting the BBQ. Turn on the gas, step back, light a match and throw it in. Wooof!  I did this one day and about 5 seconds later a mouse jumps up on the side of the BBQ, down on to the ground, and off into the bushes. I''m still not sure who was the most surprised out of the two of us.</td>', 'Good show Jason! I use the showman''s way of starting the BBQ. Turn on the gas, step back, light a match and throw it in. Wooof!  I did this one day and about 5 seconds later a mouse jumps up on the side of the BBQ, down on to the ground, and off into the bushes. I''m still not sure who was the most surprised out of the two of us.', '2003-10-23 19:51:40.000000', NULL, 0),
